==Reception==

===Critical reception===
The series received mixed reviews. Brian Lowry of ''[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]'' criticized the series, suggesting that the source material was "strained through the juvenile, rapid-fire-joke filter of ''[[Family Guy]]''", and called the show a "high-profile misfire" that didn't "bode well for Marvel's efforts to straddle the line of catering to kids without dumbing down venerable properties that plenty of adults know and love."<ref>{{cite news|last=Lowry|first=Brian|title=DXD's 'Ultimate Spider-Man' Swings ... And Misses|url=http://weblogs.variety.com/bltv/2012/03/dxds-ultimate-spider-man-swings-and-misses.html|newspaper=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=27 March 2012|access-date=11 May 2012|archive-date=17 July 2012|archive-url=https://archive.today/20120717082449/http://weblogs.variety.com/bltv/2012/03/dxds-ultimate-spider-man-swings-and-misses.html|url-status=dead}}</ref>

David Sims of ''[[The A.V. Club]]'' gave the pilot a [[Academic grading in the United States#Numerical and letter grades|"C"]] ranking, writing that the first episode "feels rather lame and perfunctory, with wackiness dialed up to 11 in an effort to distract from how fundamentally bland it is."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.avclub.com/ultimate-spider-man-ultimate-spider-man-1798172192|title=Ultimate Spider-Man debuts Sunday at 11 a.m. Eastern on Disney XD.|access-date=April 6, 2012|date=March 31, 2012|last=Sims|first=David|publisher=[[The A.V. Club]]}}</ref> Sim subsequently gave a "C+" to the episode "Doomed"<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.avclub.com/ultimate-spider-man-doomed-1798172284|title=Doomed S1 / E3|access-date=April 16, 2012|date=April 8, 2012|publisher=The A.V. Club|last=Sims|first=David}}</ref> and a "B+" to the episode "Back in Black".<ref>{{cite web|last=Sims|first=David|title=Back In Black|url=https://www.avclub.com/ultimate-spider-man-back-in-black-1798172771|publisher=The A.V. Club|date=May 13, 2012 }}</ref> Oliver Sava, also of ''The A.V. Club'', gave the episode "Venom" a "B", stating that the title of the show should be changed to ''Synergy Spider-Man'', because it goes beyond movie and [[Ultimate Marvel|Ultimate]] continuity to create an entry point for young viewers into the main line of Marvel titles.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.avclub.com/ultimate-spider-man-venom-1798172382|title=Venom S1 / E4|access-date=April 16, 2012|date=April 15, 2012|publisher=The A.V. Club|last=Sims|first=David}}</ref> Sava subsequently gave the episode "Field Trip" an "A−".<ref>{{cite web|last=Sava|first=Oliver|url=https://www.avclub.com/ultimate-spider-man-field-trip-1798172871|title=Field Trip: Ultimate Spider-Man|publisher=The A.V. Club|date=May 20, 2012}}</ref>

Emily Ashby of ''[[Common Sense Media]]'' gave the show a 4 out of 5 stars, noting the abundance of action and humor afforded by the series' premise, and opining that the lessons that Parker learns about growth and responsibility under the guidance of his mentor and friends would at least make lasting impressions on young viewers.<ref name=commonsense>{{cite web|first=Emily|last=Ashby|url=https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/ultimate-spider-man|title=Common Sense Media – Ultimate Spider-Man|access-date=April 6, 2012|publisher=[[Common Sense Media]]}}</ref>

